  "final_message": "The bug was in `cancel` in `billing/subscriptions.py`. A stray `pass` sat where the immediate-cancel path should have moved the subscription to `canceled`. Calling `cancel(..., at_period_end=False)` therefore left the subscription in its old status. Dunning then treated it as live and set it to `unpaid`, instead of marking the invoice uncollectible.\n\nI replaced the `pass` with `transition(ctx, subscription, \"canceled\")`.\n\nI added your test to `tests/test_lifecycle.py` and wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"subscriptions.py\", \"function\": \"cancel\"}`. The full suite passes (25 tests, including the new one).",
